{"collection":{"version":"1.1","href":"http://images-api.nasa.gov/search?q=Gemini+adapter+section&media_type=image&year_start=1963&year_end=1966&page_size=25","items":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-22686/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-03-01T00:00:00Z","description":"S66-22686 (March 1966) --- Mock-up of the adapter equipment section to be used on the Gemini-9 spaceflight. This section provides volume and attach points for several system modules, including Orbit Attitude Maneuver System, Environmental Control System primary oxygen supply, batteries, coolant, and electrical and electric components. This section will also hold the Astronaut Maneuvering Unit (AMU) backpack (center). Photo credit: NASA","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s66-22686","title":"GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-9 - MOCKUP - ADAPTER EQUIPMENT SECTION - FUEL CELL - MSC"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-22686/s66-22686~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1004,"size":210000,"height":1279},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-22686/s66-22686~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":502,"size":62000,"height":639},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-22686/s66-22686~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":502,"size":62000,"height":639},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-22686/s66-22686~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1506,"size":433000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-22686/s66-22686~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-57365/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-10-13T00:00:00Z","description":"S66-57365 (13 Oct. 1966) --- Astronaut Edwin E. Aldrin Jr., pilot for the Gemini-12 spaceflight, practices work tasks during zero-gravity training. He is standing in a mock-up of the Gemini spacecraft's adapter section onboard an Air Force KC-135 jet aircraft. Photo credit: NASA","keywords":["ASTRONAUT TRAINING","ASTRONAUTS","EGRESS","EXTRAVEHICULAR ACTIVITY","KC-135","GEMINI 9 FLIGHT","GEMINI PROJECT","WEIGHTLESS ENVIRONMENT TRAINING WEIGHTLESSNESS"],"media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s66-57365","title":"Astronaut Edwin Aldrin practices work task aboard KC-135"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-57365/s66-57365~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1272,"size":174000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-57365/s66-57365~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":636,"size":58000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-57365/s66-57365~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":636,"size":58000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-57365/s66-57365~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1908,"size":350000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-57365/s66-57365~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-62920/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-11-13T00:00:00Z","description":"S66-62920 (13 Nov. 1966) --- Astronaut Edwin E. Aldrin Jr., pilot of the Gemini-12 spaceflight, took this picture of the Gemini-12 spacecraft during standup extravehicular activity (EVA) with the hatch open. This is a view to the rear showing the adapter section. Photo credit: NASA","keywords":["ASTRONAUTS","EARTH OBSERVATIONS (FROM SPACE)","EXTRAVEHICULAR ACTIVITY","GEMINI 12 FLIGHT","GEMINI PROJECT","GEMINI SPACECRAFT","ONBOARD ACTIVITIES PHOTOGRAPHY"],"media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s66-62920","title":"Gemini 12 spacecraft seen during EVA"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-62920/s66-62920~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1278,"size":98000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-62920/s66-62920~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":639,"size":32000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-62920/s66-62920~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":639,"size":32000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-62920/s66-62920~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1918,"size":241000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-62920/s66-62920~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-63007/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-11-13T00:00:00Z","description":"S66-63007 (12 Nov. 1966) --- Astronaut Edwin E. Aldrin Jr., pilot of the Gemini-12 spaceflight, took this picture of the Gemini-12 spacecraft during standup extravehicular activity (EVA) with the hatch open. This is a view looking forward showing the adapter section. Photo credit: NASA","keywords":["ASTRONAUTS","EARTH OBSERVATIONS (FROM SPACE)","EXTRAVEHICULAR ACTIVITY","GEMINI 12 FLIGHT","GEMINI PROJECT","GEMINI SPACECRAFT","ONBOARD ACTIVITIES PHOTOGRAPHY"],"media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s66-63007","title":"Gemini 12 spacecraft seen during EVA"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-63007/s66-63007~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":101000,"height":1199},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-63007/s66-63007~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":33000,"height":599},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-63007/s66-63007~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":33000,"height":599},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-63007/s66-63007~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1919,"size":203000,"height":1799},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-63007/s66-63007~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-09379/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-10-01T00:00:00Z","description":"S66-09379 (1 Oct. 1966) --- Tri-Axis Magnetometer-Sensor Unit mounted on telescoping boom. Cable connects Sensor Unit with Electronics Unit mounted on retrograde beam in retrograde adapter section. Objective of experiment is to monitor the direction and amplitude of Earth's magnetic field (Gemini-12). Photo credit: NASA","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s66-09379","title":"MAGNETOMETER - TRI-AXIS SENSOR UNIT - GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-12 EXPERIMENT MSC-3 (M405) - MSC"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-09379/s66-09379~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":184000,"height":966},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-09379/s66-09379~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":63000,"height":483},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-09379/s66-09379~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":63000,"height":483},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-09379/s66-09379~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":375000,"height":1450},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-09379/s66-09379~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-09377/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-10-01T00:00:00Z","description":"S66-09377 (1 Oct. 1966) --- One of two Ion Sensors which will be used to investigate determination of Gemini-12 spacecraft attitude in yaw and pitch from measurement of ion flow variations. Each sensor is attached to an extendible boom in the retrograde adapter section. Photo credit: NASA","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s66-09377","photographer":"N/A","title":"GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-12 - EXPERIMENT D-10 - ION-SENSING ATTITUDE CONTROL - MSC"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-09377/s66-09377~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":153000,"height":977},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-09377/s66-09377~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":51000,"height":488},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-09377/s66-09377~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":51000,"height":488},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-09377/s66-09377~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1919,"size":318000,"height":1466},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-09377/s66-09377~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-32698/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-08-09T00:00:00Z","description":"S66-32698 (17 June 1966) --- Astronaut Eugene A. Cernan discusses his Gemini-9A extravehicular activity before a gathering of news media representatives in the MSC auditorium. In the background is an Astronaut Maneuvering Unit (AMU) mock-up mounted in a mock-up of a Gemini spacecraft adapter equipment section. Astronauts Cernan and Thomas P. Stafford completed their three-day mission in space on June 6, 1966. Photo credit: NASA","keywords":["ASTRONAUTS","GEMINI 10 FLIGHT","GEMINI PROJECT","PORTRAIT","SIMULATORS","TRAINING DEVICES"],"media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s66-32698","title":"Astronaut Gene Cernan poses in front of Gemini Mission Simulator"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-32698/s66-32698~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":182000,"height":828},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-32698/s66-32698~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":58000,"height":414},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-32698/s66-32698~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":58000,"height":414},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-32698/s66-32698~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":366000,"height":1242},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-32698/s66-32698~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-57326/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-10-13T00:00:00Z","description":"S66-57326 (13 Oct. 1966) --- Astronaut Edwin E. Aldrin Jr., pilot for the Gemini-12 spaceflight, attaches tether to hooks on mock-up of the adapter section of a Gemini spacecraft. He is taking part in zero-gravity training onboard an Air Force KC-135 jet aircraft in preparation for his extravehicular activity (EVA) during the actual mission. Photo credit: NASA","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s66-57326","title":"Astronaut Edwin Aldrin practices tether attachment aboard KC-135"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-57326/s66-57326~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":170000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-57326/s66-57326~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":55000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-57326/s66-57326~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":55000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-57326/s66-57326~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":344000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-57326/s66-57326~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-31665/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-05-03T00:00:00Z","description":"S66-31665 (3 May 1966) --- Astronaut Eugene A. Cernan, pilot of the Gemini-9 spaceflight, participates in extravehicular training under zero-gravity conditions aboard a KC-135 aircraft. Here, he is donning the Astronaut Maneuvering Unit (AMU) backpack after egressing a Gemini mock-up. The AMU backpack is mounted in the adapter equipment section of the mock-up. Cernan wears an extravehicular activity (EVA) life support system chest pack. Cernan will use the AMU during his scheduled EVA on the Gemini-9 mission. The KC-135 flew a parabolic curve to create the weightlessness condition for training purposes. Photo credit: NASA","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s66-31665","title":"GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-9 - TRAINING - WEIGHTLESSNESS - ASTRONAUT MANEUVERING UNIT (AMU) - ZERO-GRAVITY - FL"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-31665/s66-31665~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":192000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-31665/s66-31665~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":62000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-31665/s66-31665~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":62000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-31665/s66-31665~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":395000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-31665/s66-31665~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-54939/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-10-29T00:00:00Z","description":"S66-54939 (29 Oct. 1966) --- Astronaut Edwin E. Aldrin Jr., pilot for the Gemini-12 spaceflight, practices work tasks during underwater zero-gravity training. He is placing his feet into a special foot plate in an adapter section of the spacecraft. The foot plate will help secure him to the spacecraft during extravehicular activity (EVA). The underwater environment closely simulates the zero-gravity condition found in space. Photo credit: NASA","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s66-54939","title":"GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-12 - ASTRONAUT TRAINING - UNDERWATER - FOOT PLATES - MD"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-54939/s66-54939~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1276,"size":212000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-54939/s66-54939~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":638,"size":70000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-54939/s66-54939~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":638,"size":70000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-54939/s66-54939~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1914,"size":439000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-54939/s66-54939~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-54938/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-10-29T00:00:00Z","description":"S66-54938 (29 Oct. 1966) --- Astronaut Edwin E. Aldrin Jr., pilot for the Gemini-12 spaceflight, prepares to take a rest position during underwater zero-gravity training. His feet are secured to a mock-up of the adapter section of the spacecraft by a special foot plate. The underwater environment closely simulates the zero-gravity condition found in space. Photo credit: NASA","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s66-54938","title":"GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-12 - ASTRONAUT TRAINING - UNDERWATER - FOOT PLATES - MD"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-54938/s66-54938~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1263,"size":200000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-54938/s66-54938~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":631,"size":64000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-54938/s66-54938~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":631,"size":64000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-54938/s66-54938~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1895,"size":438000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-54938/s66-54938~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-57353/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-10-13T00:00:00Z","description":"S66-57353 (13 Oct. 1966) --- Astronaut Edwin E. Aldrin Jr., pilot for the Gemini-12 spaceflight, practices work tasks on a mock-up of the adapter section of a spacecraft. Training took place onboard an Air Force KC-135 jet aircraft. He wears a life support chest pack during the exercise. Photo credit: NASA","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s66-57353","title":"Astronaut Edwin Aldrin practices work task aboard KC-135"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-57353/s66-57353~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":160000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-57353/s66-57353~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":53000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-57353/s66-57353~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":53000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-57353/s66-57353~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":351000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-57353/s66-57353~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-05515/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-03-22T00:00:00Z","description":"S66-05515 (2 June 1966) --- Gemini-11 Experiment S-9 Nuclear Emulsion. This experiment will be used to study the cosmic radiation incident on Earth's atmosphere, to obtain detailed chemical composition of the heavy primary nuclei and to search for rare particles. Equipment is a rectangular package eight and a half by six by three inches weighing 15 pounds and including the nuclear emulsion film stack, motor to advance the emulsion and a timer to regulate the motor. The package is mounted atop the spacecraft retro adapter section prior to launch, is activated at insertion, and is retrieved by the EVA pilot. The experiment is conducted with the spacecraft in plus or minus 15 degrees of Earth's average magnetic field vector. Sponsors are NASA's Office of Space Science and Applications and the U.S. Naval Research Laboratories. Photo credit: NASA","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s66-05515","title":"GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-XI - MISC. EXPERIMENTS - MSC"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-05515/s66-05515~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":143000,"height":1092},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-05515/s66-05515~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":44000,"height":546},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-05515/s66-05515~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":44000,"height":546},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-05515/s66-05515~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":327000,"height":1639},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-05515/s66-05515~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]}],"metadata":{"total_hits":13}}}